# Terraform state records real resource ids and, for some resource types,
# secrets. This configuration creates no secret-bearing resource — there are no
# access keys anywhere in the design, which is #173's whole point — but state is
# still not repository content: it is a live record of one account.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfstate.backup
crash.log
crash.*.log

# Provider plugins and the lock's local cache.
.terraform/

# Saved plans can embed variable values.
*.tfplan

# Real variable values. terraform.tfvars.example is committed; the real one is
# not, so an operator can point this at a different account without a diff.
*.auto.tfvars
terraform.tfvars

# Everything else here is source, including .terraform.lock.hcl, which is
# committed on purpose so a reviewer's plan resolves the same provider build.
